From 517fffc6ac5da47a72a6279c915d34377536864d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shahriar Iravanian <siravan@svtsim.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 21:59:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01/12] rusticol: tile-override feature (RUSTICOL_TILE_POINTS)

New cargo feature `tile-override` (off by default). With RUSTICOL_TILE_POINTS=N,
compiled-direct engines whose cache-sized reduction tile is 1 point run with
execution and reduction tiles of N points instead; other engines are unchanged.
Large processes (e.g. u u~ > Z + 6g) spend much less time per point in the
reduction with N in the thousands, and N is the batch a GPU runner sees.

Also fixes rustfmt in evaluation.rs, helicity_lane.rs and reduction.rs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
